Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• `event_date`: limit the scan to December 2020 (`'20201201'–'20201231'`).  
• `event_name`: keep only purchase‑type events (`'purchase'`).  
• `items` (ARRAY of STRUCTs) – the array that actually lists the products bought in each event.  
  – `items.item_name`: look for `'Google Navy Speckled Tee'` and for every other product bought in the same event.  
  – `items.quantity`: add up the quantities to see which companion product has the highest total quantity.  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX` (automatically supplied when a wildcard table is used): lets us scan all December 2020 daily tables at once.

Principal conditions that will be reused  

1. `_TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'` — December 2020 only.  
2. `event_name = 'purchase'` — purchase events only.  
3. `EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM UNNEST(items) i WHERE i.item_name = 'Google Navy Speckled Tee')` — keep only those purchase events that contain the tee.  
4. When we unnest the items array again, ignore the tee itself so we can rank the “other” products (`WHERE i.item_name <> 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'`).

Below are ten exploratory → progressively more complex queries (all limited to 20 rows, except the last one that already gives the single answer).  
Replace or remove the LIMIT clause when you need the full result set.

```sql
-- 1. Distinct event names that appear in December 2020
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Sample of purchase events (event_timestamp and number of array elements)
SELECT event_timestamp,
       ARRAY_LENGTH(items) AS items_in_event
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Show the first 20 purchase events that contain the Navy Speckled Tee
SELECT event_timestamp,
       event_date,
       i.item_name,
       i.quantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND i.item_name = 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Distinct product names that ever appear together with the Tee
SELECT DISTINCT i.item_name AS companion_product
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*` t
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM UNNEST(t.items) AS tee
        WHERE tee.item_name = 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
      ),
     UNNEST(t.items) AS i
WHERE i.item_name <> 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Quantities of every product inside ONE sample event that had the Tee
SELECT event_timestamp,
       i.item_name,
       i.quantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*` t,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM UNNEST(t.items) tee
        WHERE tee.item_name = 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
      )
ORDER BY event_timestamp
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. How many purchase events include the Tee?
SELECT COUNT(*) AS purchase_events_with_tee
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM UNNEST(items) tee
        WHERE tee.item_name = 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
      );
```

```sql
-- 7. Total quantity of each companion product (pre‑aggregated per event)
SELECT i.item_name,
       SUM(i.quantity) AS total_quantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*` t,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM UNNEST(t.items) tee
        WHERE tee.item_name = 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
      )
  AND i.item_name <> 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
GROUP BY i.item_name
ORDER BY total_quantity DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as #7, but also list number of unique purchase events where the product co‑occurred
SELECT i.item_name,
       COUNT(DISTINCT t.event_timestamp) AS purchase_events,
       SUM(i.quantity)                    AS total_quantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*` t,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM UNNEST(t.items) tee
        WHERE tee.item_name = 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
      )
  AND i.item_name <> 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
GROUP BY i.item_name
ORDER BY total_quantity DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Verify one more time which item ranks #1 by quantity
SELECT i.item_name,
       SUM(i.quantity) AS total_quantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*` t,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM UNNEST(t.items) tee
        WHERE tee.item_name = 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
      )
  AND i.item_name <> 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
GROUP BY i.item_name
ORDER BY total_quantity DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: the single product bought with the highest total quantity next to the Navy Speckled Tee in Dec‑2020
SELECT i.item_name                   AS most_common_companion_product,
       SUM(i.quantity)               AS total_quantity_with_tee
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*` t,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM UNNEST(t.items) tee
        WHERE tee.item_name = 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
      )
  AND i.item_name <> 'Google Navy Speckled Tee'
GROUP BY i.item_name
ORDER BY total_quantity_with_tee DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

